fix.summary:
I checked all three review findings against the code. All three were real, and I fixed each one with tests, without touching any file outside my stream. 236 tests pass across the 10 suites that cover these routes. tsc is clean for my files and shows 0 errors overall.

1. W3B-RV-1 (Module Access did not close the newly opened routes). I added a gate that checks the role's modules on the routes this pass opened. It uses the same source of truth as the central gate (`effectiveModulesForUser`), refuses on any error, and skips the manager tiers, which had no module check before. It lives in /home/user/servd/backend/src/modules/opex/moduleGate.ts. Applied:
   - every /opex route needs 'capital';
   - petty-cash boxes (list, create, reconcile) and deposit drops (GET and POST) need 'accounting'. Petty-cash movements are not gated and stay open to all staff;
   - the staff-meal log needs 'staff_directory';
   - positions reads (list, summary, departments, shift bands) and the contributions list need 'staff_directory' or 'capital';
   - every positions and shift-band write needs 'staff_directory'.
   The prefix rules in moduleAccess.ts are no longer needed for this fix; they are an optional follow-up (see needsOtherFiles).

2. W3B-RV-2 (finance could see full gift-card codes). For roles outside the manager tiers, the list now shows the code as '••••' plus its last 4 characters, and blanks buyerEmail, recipientEmail, buyerCustomerId and message. The card's code is masked the same way in /gift-cards/:id/redemptions. Managers still see the full card. The admin page needs no change: it shows whatever code comes back, and the 'via email' line disappears when the email is null.

3. W3B-RV-3 (positions accepted another company's shift band). checkSeatRefs now checks shiftBandId: it must be a band of the seat's own company, otherwise 422 SHIFT_BAND_NOT_IN_COMPANY. This applies to both POST and PATCH. A new band must not be archived. A PATCH that re-sends the seat's current band is still accepted after that band is archived, because the edit form always sends shiftBandId and every save would otherwise fail. A band from another company is refused even if it is the seat's current one.
